<!--
	The ids of rules and schedule entries become references (haumacher/ehome #90): the datapoint of a
	trigger or action, the output of a schedule entry, the entry of a schedule trigger, the timer and
	the parameter of a trigger or action. A property changing into a reference of the same name would
	be deleted with its values and created again by the automatic model upgrade. Here the SQL first
	moves the id texts of these objects (in every revision) to flex attributes of their own,
	issue90.<attribute>; then the properties are deleted from the stored model and the references
	created as the model declares them, and the rules become datapoints (their enable switch). After
	the start, the startup action RuleReferenceMigration resolves each moved id in its project (a
	timer or parameter in its rule) and sets the reference; an id naming nothing of the project leaves
	the reference empty and is logged. The history keeps the old texts in the flex attributes until
	the action removes them from the current state.
-->
